\begin{align*}
|z| &= \sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\\
&= 13.
\end{align*}
Since the magnitude of $z$ is 13, we have $a^2 + b^2 = 13^2 = 169.$  Now,
\begin{align*}
z \times \overline{z} &= (a+bi)(a-bi)\\
&= a^2 + b^2\\
&= 169.
\end{align*}
Therefore, $z \times \overline{z} = 169.$ </think> <answer> 169 </answer>

